diff --git a/api-ref/source/v3/checkpoints.inc b/api-ref/source/v3/checkpoints.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0fa99be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/api-ref/source/v3/checkpoints.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+.. -*- rst -*-
+
+Native checkpoint service contract (private 3.72)
+=================================================
+
+This is a private extension of this fork, requiring microversion 3.72. It is
+not the upstream API with the same version number. It coordinates disk
+snapshots for a future Nova RAM checkpoint workflow; it does not save RAM.
+
+Every request requires the project user's token and a verified service token.
+The service user must be in ``[checkpoint] nova_service_user_ids``. Project
+member/admin policy is necessary but cannot substitute for service identity.
+An operation is readable and replayable only by its original project, user,
+and service user, including when the caller is an administrator.
+
+Reserve a checkpoint operation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /v3/{project_id}/checkpoint-operations
+
+Reserve every volume atomically. ``kind`` is ``create``, ``revert``, or
+``delete``. Create requires one attached volume per disk, all attached to the
+specified instance. The list must contain 1 to 64 unique UUIDs. The configured
+limit may be lower. Revert/delete require exactly the saved checkpoint volume
+set; the server selects snapshot IDs from its journal.
+
+``request_id`` provides durable idempotency. An exact replay returns the same
+operation after release or snapshot deletion. Reusing it with another payload
+returns 409. A checkpoint UUID cannot be reused after deletion or abort.
+
+Normal response code: 202. Errors: 400 schema, 403 authorization, 404 resource
+not found or not owned, 409 conflict/unsupported backend, 413 quota, and 503
+backend unavailable. No supported driver is enabled by this patch alone.
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+   - project_id: project_id_path
+   - checkpoint_operation: checkpoint_operation
+   - request_id: checkpoint_request_id
+   - checkpoint_id: checkpoint_id
+   - instance_uuid: checkpoint_instance_uuid
+   - kind: checkpoint_kind
+   - volume_ids: checkpoint_volume_ids
+
+Request example
+---------------
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/checkpoints/checkpoint-create-request.json
+   :language: javascript
+
+Response example
+----------------
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/checkpoints/checkpoint-create-response.json
+   :language: javascript
+
+Read an operation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/{project_id}/checkpoint-operations/{operation_id}
+
+Returns 200 with ``checkpoint_operation``. Resources contain Cinder volume,
+snapshot and association UUIDs, size and status. Steps contain their UUID,
+resource UUID, phase, generation, status and a safe error code. Backend native
+IDs/references, credentials, quota reservations and raw errors are never part
+of this response. A foreign or missing operation returns 404.
+
+List operations
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/{project_id}/checkpoint-operations
+
+Returns 200 with ``checkpoint_operations`` and pagination links if needed.
+Only the original project/user/service identity's operations are listed.
+Filters: ``checkpoint_id``, ``instance_uuid``, ``status``; pagination:
+``marker`` and ``limit``. Unknown parameters return 400. Tombstones remain
+visible. The list does not expose another user's operations to project admin.
+
+Operate on a reservation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /v3/{project_id}/checkpoint-operations/{operation_id}/action
+
+The body contains exactly one of ``execute``, ``reconcile``, ``cleanup``,
+``release``. Each takes integer ``generation`` (1 in C1). Release additionally
+takes ``outcome`` equal to ``commit`` or ``abort``. The response is 202 with the
+current operation; asynchronous dispatch is not proof of backend completion.
+Poll the operation and its steps.
+
+* ``execute`` dispatches each prepared native step at most once. Revert requires
+  every volume to be available and without attachments.
+* ``reconcile`` queries pending/unknown results without replaying an effect.
+* ``cleanup`` applies only to an unfinished create after every create outcome
+  is known. It cancels undispatched steps and creates separate native delete
+  steps for confirmed snapshots. Repetition keeps the same step UUIDs.
+* ``release(commit)`` requires all steps to have succeeded. Revert additionally
+  requires completed attachments to the original instance and in-use volumes.
+* ``release(abort)`` is allowed before effects, or after confirmed create
+  cleanup. Partial revert, unknown outcomes or unfinished cleanup return 409.
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/checkpoints/checkpoint-execute-request.json
+   :language: javascript
+
+States: ``reserved``, ``running``, ``succeeded``, ``failed``,
+``recovery_required``, ``released``. Step states: ``prepared``, ``dispatching``,
+``pending``, ``succeeded``, ``failed_no_effect``, ``unknown``. Disabling new
+checkpoints, elapsed time, restart and query success never release ownership.
+There is no force-unlock, ownership transfer or automatic retry of an effect.
+
+Query a volume's capabilities
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/{project_id}/volumes/{volume_id}/checkpoint-capabilities
+
+Returns 200 with ``checkpoint_capabilities`` for the current backend. The
+contract version is 1. Required booleans are ``native_snapshot``,
+``arbitrary_inplace_revert``, ``preserves_other_checkpoints``,
+``independent_snapshot_delete`` and ``operation_reconciliation``.
+``snapshot_semantics`` must be ``cow`` or ``row``; neither is inferred from a
+product name. ``consistent_group_snapshot`` is optional for support and is
+reported explicitly. ``driver_identity`` contains driver class, driver version
+and validated profile. Invalid/unverified capabilities return
+``supported=false`` with safe ``unsupported_reasons``. All existing production
+drivers report unsupported until a separately validated adapter implements
+this contract. In particular, this patch does not certify Dorado or TATLIN.
+
+Attachment scope
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The existing attachment create/update/delete/complete APIs accept
+``OpenStack-Checkpoint-Operation-ID`` and
+``OpenStack-Checkpoint-Generation`` together at microversion 3.72. They require
+the same service authorization and owner identity as the operation. Headers
+alone provide no authorization. Disconnect is limited to original attachments
+of the reserved revert. Reconnect is permitted only after all native reverts
+succeed, to the original instance. Volume UUIDs are preserved; new attachment
+UUIDs are expected. Old microversions reject these headers. Legacy
+initialize/terminate connection APIs have no checkpoint bypass.
