+---
+features:
+  - |
+    Adds a disabled-by-default private Cinder checkpoint service contract:
+    API 3.72, Volume RPC 3.21 and object manifest 1.40. It provides durable
+    all-volume ownership, native-only execution, query-based reconciliation,
+    scoped attachments, idempotent quotas and protected checkpoint snapshots.
+    Existing drivers remain unsupported. Nova RAM integration and validated
+    Huawei Dorado/YADRO TATLIN adapters are separate work.
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    Apply migration 7fa82e10c601 and upgrade every Cinder resource writer before
+    enabling checkpoints. Configure verified Nova service tokens and the
+    checkpoint nova_service_user_ids allowlist. RPC gates do not detect old
+    API processes. Downgrade requires all operations and references cleaned up.
+security:
+  - |
+    Tenant metadata, administrator status and tenant service roles cannot
+    bypass checkpoint ownership. Unknown native outcomes retain protection;
+    no timeout-based unlock or copy fallback is provided.
